<title>FRANCE: Cogema, Chugoku renew uranium contract.</title>
<headline>Cogema, Chugoku renew uranium contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>French nuclear engineering group Cogema said on Tuesday it signed a contract with Chugoku Electric Power Co Inc of Japan, renewing an agreement on uranium enrichment to 2006.</p>
<p>Chugoku, based in Hiroshima, runs two nuclear reactors and plans a third facility, Cogema said in a statement. Cogema gave no value for the contract. It said Japan accounts for about 12 percent of its annual turnover.</p>
</text>
